Accept MLS commits that remove a leaf for which the backend has no member row, as left behind by the member row loss fixed in WPB-29648, instead of rejecting them with `mls-invalid-leaf-node-index`. Such a leaf is checked against the ratchet tree of the stored group info: it must not be blank, and an external commit may only remove the sender's own leaf, and only if the sender has no member row. Affected clients can now be removed by other members and re-join with an external commit; previously the failed re-join could make clients retry endlessly. External commits removing the history client are now rejected as well.
